I've written the Day 246 (20:08) assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as c309f3bf. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I committed it with -f, the same way earlier sessions committed their assessments.

Build and runs
• The harness found the build green at ca821ce0, and CI passed on the last 5 pushes.
• I ran the binary and yoyo -p answered pong (exit 0).
• One recent evolve run failed on Oct 31 at 19:41, about a minute in at the "Cache cargo" step. That's an infrastructure failure, not code.
• No reverts in the last 14 days.

Main finding: one function causes most of #1111. I ran every shell verb with --bogus in a fresh temp repo:
• Carry on with exit 0: init, status, version, help, doctor and evolution. init --bogus actually wrote a YOYO.md.
• Exit 1: docs looked --bogus up on docs.rs, and changelog just failed on not being in a git repo.
• Already refuse with exit 2: tree, log, lint, risk, undo, diff, commit and skill.
• The cause: positional_after_verb (src/dispatch_sub.rs:141) drops any word that starts with - without checking it against KNOWN_FLAGS, so the stray-word refusal never sees it. With a plain word instead (status stray), those verbs do exit 2.
• The fix: one fix in that function would cover about 9 verbs at once, instead of another one-verb slice.
• Correction to #1111: it lists find as already refusing, but find --bogus exits 0 and searches for it. memories and docs do the same, because they take free text, so each needs its own decision on whether --bogus is a search term.

Other things for the planner
• Two files close to the size limit: src/config.rs is 11 lines away. src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines away and not on the size exemption list. A task that crosses the limit fails cargo test and gets reverted.
• #1113 is still live: yoyo -p --help prints help instead of sending --help as the prompt.
• A test name states something we disproved on Day 239: post_hook_feedback_reaches_the_model_as_its_own_tool_result_block says the feedback is "its own block", which was measured false. It should be renamed.
• `CLAUDE_CODE_GAP.md` is out of date: its header hasn't been re-verified in 172 days.

Research (saved to yopedia)
• Claude Code 2.1.314–316:
  • It added a setting that blocks writes outside the working directory, which matches the opt-in YOYO_BLOCK_OUTSIDE_WRITES we shipped on Day 245.
  • It added a separate effort setting for sub-agents. We have a sub-agent model setting but none for effort; I haven't checked whether our sub-agents inherit the main effort.
  • It fixed shell commands left running when it exits on its own, which is the same problem as our open #1100.
• Codex CLI: an unknown argument exits 2 with a hint to use -- --x if you meant it as text. That's the convention the #1111 fix should follow.
